  "mechanisms": [
    "Actor-private tickets fix expected size/hash, mount authority revision, destination, parent identity/revision and persistent store UUID. Request JSON cannot supply these authority/storage snapshots.",
    "New chunks are immutable generated objects, length/digest checked, sealed and synced before checkpoint event/reference/offset/receipt commit. SQL enforces contiguous extension and defers commit until the chunk row exists.",
    "All thirteen domain relations are checked/locked per scoped transaction. Owned tickets/receipts are actor-private; a full-root inspector can account for chunk metadata without downloading unaccepted bytes.",
    "Transactions and immutable object IDs fence synchronous checkpoint requests; lost transactions may leave separate orphans but cannot move the offset or mutate a recorded chunk. Background-worker lease qualification remains separate.",
    "Concurrent same-offset requests have one winner. Exact retries return original receipts; wrong offsets, changed meanings, invalid body hashes and foreign actors are denied.",
    "Storage marker initialization publishes a synced UUID atomically. Separate roots reject ticket continuation. Missing/corrupt IDs are preserved and rejected; read-only opening never initializes a store.",
    "Each new write rechecks current destination permission and pinned parent revision. Completion also rechecks target revision; destination replacement, folder revocation and changed bytes cannot publish.",
    "Completion verifies each recorded chunk, assembles with bounded buffers/descriptors and checks the entire expected hash before syncing and atomically committing file acceptance, namespace publication, completed session and receipt.",
    "SFTP ticket stat exposes only durable progress; get is denied. Uncommitted in-memory tails are dropped. Successful close or explicit completion verifies/publishes; control rename can only finalize the bound destination."
  ],
  "migration_notes": [
    "Migration 5 adds tickets/checkpoints/receipts and reserves the live control namespace while preserving deleted namespace history.",
    "Migration 5 was already applied when the wrong-storage-root failure was reproduced. Its checksum stayed frozen; migration 6 adds immutable storage binding.",
    "Previously experimental unbound tickets remain unbound. No store is inferred, no orphan adopted and no history rewritten. Reviewed recovery/rebinding remains open."
  ],
